   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Known hole: a one-way push that pauses, then the set's first drive, is one swing to this detector.\nThe speed goes out past +0.30, turns at the top, and comes back past -0.30, which is the shape of a rep.\nWhat separates them is the travel the push leaves behind, and this detector does not measure travel.",
   "originalText": "Known hole: a one-way push that pauses, then the set's first drive, is one swing to this detector.\nThe speed goes out past +0.30, turns at the top, and comes back past -0.30, which is the shape of a rep.\nWhat separates them is the travel the push leaves behind, and this detector does not measure travel.",
   "fontSize": 15,
